  <main>
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Cat care FAQ</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Curious about cats?</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Quick answers for common feline mysteries, from slow blinks and kneading
        to feeding habits and indoor enrichment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq-card" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
          Why do cats purr?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but purring can also be a
              self-soothing behavior when they are stressed, uncomfortable, or healing.
              Context and body language help reveal what the purr means.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
          How much sleep do cats need?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              Most adult cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, while kittens and senior
              cats may sleep even more. Their crepuscular rhythm means they are
              naturally more active around dawn and dusk.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
          Why does my cat knead blankets or my lap?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              Kneading is a comforting behavior that begins in kittenhood. Adult
              cats often knead when they feel secure, mark a soft spot with scent
              glands in their paws, or settle in for a cozy nap.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
          Should cats live indoors or outdoors?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              Indoor cats are generally safer from traffic, predators, disease, and
              harsh weather. They still need stimulation, so provide climbing spaces,
              scratching posts, window views, puzzle feeders, and regular play.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
          What does a slow blink from a cat mean?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              A slow blink is often a friendly, relaxed signal. You can slowly blink
              back to communicate calmly, but let the cat choose whether to approach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-6" id="question-6">
          How often should I play with my cat?
          <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-6">
          <div class="details-inner">
            <p>
              Aim for a few short play sessions every day. Wand toys, chase games,
              and puzzle feeders help satisfy hunting instincts and can reduce
              boredom-related behavior.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <script>
    const examples = document.querySelectorAll(".example");

    examples.forEach((example) => {
      const button = example.querySelector(".question");
      const details = example.querySelector(".details");

      button.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const isOpen = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isOpen));
        example.classList.toggle("is-open", !isOpen);
        details.style.maxHeight = isOpen ? "0" : `${details.scrollHeight}px`;
      });
    });

    window.addEventListener("resize", () => {
      examples.forEach((example) => {
        const button = example.querySelector(".question");
        const details = example.querySelector(".details");

        if (button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true") {
          details.style.maxHeight = `${details.scrollHeight}px`;
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
